    "text": "Two particles of masses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are initially at rest at an infinite distance apart. If they approach each other under their mutual interaction given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>.&nbsp;Their speed of approach at the instant when they are at a distance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> apart is",
