  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi></math>&nbsp;be the reduced mass of the system and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></math>&nbsp;be the approach speed of the particles, then</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>&#956;v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></msubsup><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mi>dr</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mfrac><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></math></p>",
